# Tech Stack

- FastAPI
- Python
- PostgreSQL
- SQLAlchemy (Async ORM)
- Alembic
- Pydantic
- OAuth2 + JWT
- LangChain
- Groq LLM
- AsyncIO
- HTTPX

---

# Architecture

The project follows a layered architecture:

```text
Client
    │
    ▼
FastAPI Routes
    │
    ▼
Business Services
    │
    ▼
AI Layer
    │
    ▼
LLM
```

Supporting components include:

- Authentication Layer
- Global Exception Handler
- Structured Logging
- Validation Layer
- Database Layer

This separation keeps business logic independent from routing while making the codebase easier to extend and maintain.

---

# Design Principles

- Separation of Concerns
- Async-first architecture
- Production-oriented code organization
- Strong typing with Pydantic
- Centralized error handling
- Consistent API responses
- Structured logging
- Dependency Injection
- Reusable AI services

---

# Running the Project

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Floats-del/blog-ai-service-developing.git
```

Create a virtual environment:

```bash
python -m venv .venv
```

Activate it:

Windows

```bash
.venv\Scripts\activate
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Configure your environment variables:

```env
DATABASE_URL=
SECRET_KEY=
ALGORITHM=
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=
GROQ_API_KEY=
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
```

Run migrations:

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

Start the server:

```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

